{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/27","id":4516856640,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUSya2c8AAAABDTnDQA","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/27","diff_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/27.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/27.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/issues/27","number":27,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Formalize specialization and connect the original theta source to Hochschild trace","user":{"login":"KokunoYumeto","id":208192274,"node_id":"U_kgDODGjDEg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208192274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Source-preserving continuation\n\nThis draft joins the owner's specialization/curvature construction to Connes–Consani, *Hochschild homology, trace map and zeta-cycles* (2023), pp. 83–101. It retains the original theta source, infinite split-zero coefficient quotient, arithmetic action, Gram metric, full nilpotent jets, and the distinction between supported zero and external absence.\n\n**Final diff: 16 added files, no modified or deleted files**, checked against current main `e4ee97cdce904d4b9bb5697d33095aaa00083f24`. Main incorporated PR26 during this continuation. The branch was then integrated with that complete current-main tree, preserving its publication, index and archive changes rather than restoring older versions. The current head is `a4a87844c257485ae6d669f5b3eb6d96b9e8b8d8`. `COORDINATION.md` records the reconciliation. This session has not merged PR27 or changed main.\n\n## Observed verification\n\n[Successful run 34735210715](https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/actions/runs/34735210715), job `103665300994`, checked source commit `25960903723954d6118b1aa76a817cb6a7f452f0`. All five new Lean modules and four inherited restriction modules passed separate `--trust=0 -DwarningAsError=true` checks. Joint imports and exact-target transitive audits passed for **38 new** and **33 inherited** declarations. The allowlist is `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\nThe new exact checkers passed **17 + 10 test methods** normally and under `python -O`, with identical records; both deliberate negative controls failed in both modes. The unchanged 16-method restriction suite, rational enclosure example, and 13-check zero-mode fixture also passed fresh replays. Lean remains 4.31.0 and Mathlib remains pinned to `fabf563a7c95a166b8d7b6efca11c8b4dc9d911f`.\n\nThe documentation and concurrent-main integration change none of the five verified Lean blobs, either checker, the audits, or the workflow. The inherited formal tree is exactly the already inspected PR26 tree. `STATUS.md` and `VALIDATION.json` identify the actual observed checkpoint; a later unobserved run is not silently claimed.\n\n## Mathematical contents\n\n`HOCHSCHILD_COMPARISON.md` proves the literal theta/Hochschild trace factorization, retaining the factor two and the half-density isometry. The original Gaussian seed is exactly the image of `D^2-D`. The resulting two-term and ordered-two-leg comparisons retain the original supported complex.\n\nIt constructs the actual full-to-critical Schwartz quotient map and calculates its kernel on every specified finite arithmetic packet: precisely the off-critical generalized blocks. Critical blocks have explicit jet retractions with the phase `i^(-j)/j!`. This distinguishes the chapter's all-zero realization from its critical-only realization instead of inferring injectivity from the latter.\n\nThe note documents a qualification in the printed raw-section assertion at the Scaling Site boundary: the original seed has zeroth Fourier coefficient `xi(1/2)/sqrt(L)`, which does not extend to zero. A renormalized zero line is retained separately, and an explicit Gaussian average of original source dilates shows how that line becomes a closed supported boundary. This is a written analytic repair requiring independent review, not a claim that the entire published theorem has been disproved or Lean-verified.\n\n`SplitZeroLaplacianControl.lean` proves the exact original-metric adjoint and energy identities, constituent intertwining, full quadratic jets, and the generalized-block vanishing lemma. `LAPLACIAN_PARABOLA.md` gives a written quantitative enclosure of the full original-metric numerical range from a two-sided weight-defect bound; that completing-square estimate is not in the Lean scope.\n\n`RESEARCH_NOTE.md` connects four specialization modules with the cyclic gcd description of the least invariant enlargement, its signed metric-pole curvature contribution, and the original trace-only curvature-cost certificate. Global sheaves, curvature currents, all-order derivative interpretation, and the logarithmic integral retain written-proof scope.\n\n## Review boundary\n\nNo uniform arithmetic upper-volume/nonconcentration estimate, invariant positive metric, spectral simplicity, or RH conclusion is asserted. No local runtime execution or replay of the uploaded 23-method archive is claimed. The analytic Schwartz, heat-limit, and coherent-sheaf arguments are distinct from the successfully checked Lean and finite symbolic statements. Existing source attribution and rights remain unchanged.","created_at":"2026-09-13T03:28:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T03:31:42Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"59b5aadebcf91350430c0eba30ae6bae4087738d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/27/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/27/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/issues/27/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/statuses/a4a87844c257485ae6d669f5b3eb6d96b9e8b8d8","head":{"label":"KokunoYumeto:astra/specialization-curvature-20260913","ref":"astra/specialization-curvature-20260913","sha":"a4a87844c257485ae6d669f5b3eb6d96b9e8b8d8","user":{"login":"KokunoYumeto","id":208192274,"node_id":"U_kgDODGjDEg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208192274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kokuno